  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member who folds the iPhone Duo (or resizes the iPad window across regular width) while a composer is open over a topic, I want the page to stay usable afterwards. Today the reader can keep thinking a composer is open, so its taps are ignored, the back button is hidden and \"Répondre\" stays off.\n\n### Scenario (read from the code, not run on a device)\nA reply, edit or MP composer is open over a topic. The member folds the Duo or resizes the iPad window across regular width:\n- `RootNavigationView` swaps the root, and `NavigationModel.reader(for:)` hands the same `TopicReaderModel` to a new `TopicReaderView`.\n- The old view goes away without reporting its composer closed: `TopicReaderModel.openComposers` is fed only by the views' `onChange` (`ReaderComposerGuard`, `ReaderReplyFlow`, `ReaderAuthorMenuSheet`).\n- So `suspendsPageInteractions` stays true on the shared reader until another topic is selected.\n\n### Sources\n- Found by the Fable review of #1241 (round 2), as a hole of `dev-swift`, not of that PR: https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/1241\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderModel+Composer.swift` (`ReaderComposerGuard`, `suspendsPageInteractions`), `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderModel.swift` `composer(_:isOpen:)`.\n\n### Fix idea (from the review)\nMake each view's report authoritative when it appears: `.onChange(of: isEditing, initial: true)` in `ReaderComposerGuard`, and the same for the reply and the author menu's MP. A newly shown view then corrects a stale entry.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- A test: a reader with a stale `.edit` (or `.reply`) entry, a fresh report saying closed: the slot is free again.\n- A check on the device (#893 list): fold the Duo with a composer open, unfold, the page responds.",
